---
description: General project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Core Principles

- Write clean, simple, production-ready code.
- Keep responses concise.
- Modify existing code instead of rewriting whole files.
- Reuse existing components, hooks, and utilities.
- Never add code that was not requested.
- Preserve existing functionality.
- Do not rename files unless requested.

# Code Quality

- Add concise doc comments above functions, components, and hooks.
- Include @param tags when parameters exist.
- Keep files focused.
- Avoid duplicate logic.
- Remove unused imports and variables.

# Scope

- Change only what the task requires.
- Do not add unrelated refactors.
- Do not create fake data.
- Do not commit secrets.

# Response Style

Before coding:
1. Understand existing implementation.
2. Check related files.
3. Make the smallest possible change.

Do not explain obvious code.
Do not repeat the whole file.
Only show changed sections unless full file is requested.